# Normalize line endings so a fresh clone is runnable on any platform.
# core.autocrlf=true stores LF in the repo but would hand a .sh file CRLF on
# checkout -- and a "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" shebang will not execute. Pin the
# EOL each file type actually needs; comments must sit on their own lines here.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must always be LF (a CRLF shebang fails: bad interpreter).
*.sh   text eol=lf

# Windows batch wants CRLF; LF tolerates on modern cmd, but be explicit and correct.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf

# The log and profile artifacts are LF on every platform.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
